WEBVTT

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:07.440
It's 03:00 we call it to order. Our first order of business is the COVID-nineteen

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.440
town of Andover information

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:10.480
briefing.

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:12.240
Eric would you like to proceed?

00:00:13.345 --> 00:00:14.225
>> Sure.

00:00:14.865 --> 00:00:19.505
As you know, we're kind of in the midst of a pandemic.

00:00:20.065 --> 00:00:23.585
So far, Andover has been relatively unscathed.

00:00:23.585 --> 00:00:24.945
We have no reports,

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:28.440
no reported cases of COVID-nineteen

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:29.800
in Andover.

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:36.760
That doesn't mean we don't have any. It just means nobody here has gotten tested and has tested positive.

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:41.555
So I sent some information to the board earlier,

00:00:42.035 --> 00:00:44.195
which was just the

00:00:45.155 --> 00:00:46.355
extrapolated

00:00:46.355 --> 00:00:47.235
data

00:00:47.235 --> 00:00:50.595
basically from the cases so far in Connecticut,

00:00:51.635 --> 00:00:55.900
both of the number of people who were sick and also the number of dead.

00:00:56.380 --> 00:00:57.260
You can

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:01.740
consider that or not as at your leisure.

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:04.380
So what the town has done

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:07.420
is done two things. The first is

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:09.500
prioritize

00:01:09.705 --> 00:01:11.785
putting in place a mechanism

00:01:11.785 --> 00:01:19.385
for food and food distribution to those that most need it, which tend to be the people that

00:01:19.865 --> 00:01:22.745
have been needing the food bank services.

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:27.940
As many of you know, we've shut down senior transportation

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:30.980
because it's basically impossible to do

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:32.100
a

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:33.940
reasonable job of

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:35.060
social

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:36.260
distancing

00:01:35.955 --> 00:01:39.715
if you're transporting multiple people in vehicles.

00:01:40.195 --> 00:01:41.715
So we have instead

00:01:42.035 --> 00:01:47.955
switched to a mechanism for delivery of food to those people who use senior transportation

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:50.480
to get food in the past.

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:55.120
And we also have an arrangement in place with Ted's Market

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:56.960
and the CERT team.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:57.920
So

00:01:58.240 --> 00:01:59.520
they're basically,

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:03.865
you can call into the town, you'll be relayed to the CERT team,

00:02:04.265 --> 00:02:07.625
and you'll be able to essentially order food

00:02:08.105 --> 00:02:09.785
through Ted's market

00:02:09.865 --> 00:02:17.400
and have it delivered. And this again is a service for people who either are getting sick and really can't be out and about

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:21.480
or are in an elderly really high risk category

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:25.560
and don't have any family member that can supply them with food.

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:26.520
So

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:32.735
we're doing what we can to supply services to those people that need it the most.

00:02:33.935 --> 00:02:35.775
We are also at this point

00:02:36.095 --> 00:02:39.055
keeping the majority of town employees

00:02:39.055 --> 00:02:40.575
working from home

00:02:41.055 --> 00:02:45.295
and we've done two things with that. One, we've had our IT provider

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:50.820
install the firewalls that we were purchasing anyway

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:54.580
as part of the up the IT upgrade to the down mall.

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:56.100
And Excuse

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:00.020
the second thing is that

00:03:01.385 --> 00:03:07.625
we're enabling the off the employees to be able to remote into the office and work from home.

00:03:08.025 --> 00:03:10.665
And the way it's working is that employees

00:03:10.745 --> 00:03:14.620
are not prohibited from coming to the town hall. They're

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:21.020
all having to come to the town hall at least a couple times a week to get what they need to do business,

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:24.220
but to do as much of their work from home

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:25.660
whenever they can.

00:03:26.915 --> 00:03:29.875
So that's most of what we've been doing

00:03:30.195 --> 00:03:32.355
on the town side.

00:03:32.755 --> 00:03:36.115
